---
title: Sequence Diagram — Article Creation (Full Event-Driven Flow)
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor Author as 👤 Author
    participant React as React SPA
    participant GW as API Gateway
    participant KC as Keycloak
    participant AS as Article Service
    participant PG as PostgreSQL
    participant REDIS as Redis Cache
    participant KAFKA as Kafka
    participant AIS as AI/LLM Service
    participant SS as Search Service
    participant ANS as Analytics Service
    participant NS as Notification Service

    Note over Author,NS: Phase 1: Authentication + Article Creation

    Author->>React: Write article in rich editor
    React->>KC: Check JWT token validity
    KC-->>React: Token valid (role: EDITOR)
    React->>GW: POST /api/v1/articles<br/>Authorization: Bearer {JWT}<br/>{title, content, categoryId, tags[]}

    GW->>KC: Validate JWT signature + expiry
    KC-->>GW: Token valid, claims: {sub, role: EDITOR}
    GW->>GW: Circuit Breaker check (Resilience4j)
    GW->>AS: Forward with user context

    Note over AS,PG: Phase 2: DDD Domain Processing

    AS->>AS: Validate CreateArticleRequest
    AS->>AS: Article.create(title, content, author, category)<br/>Aggregate Root factory method
    AS->>AS: Article.addTags(tags)<br/>Business rule: max 10 tags
    AS->>AS: Domain Events registered:<br/>1. ArticleCreatedEvent<br/>2. ArticleTaggedEvent
    AS->>PG: INSERT INTO articles<br/>(content stored as TEXT,<br/>metadata as JSONB)
    PG-->>AS: Article saved (UUID)

    AS->>REDIS: INVALIDATE cache key:<br/>articles:list:*
    AS->>KAFKA: Publish ArticleCreatedEvent<br/>Topic: article-events<br/>{articleId, title, authorId, tags, content}

    AS-->>GW: 201 Created + ArticleResponse
    GW-->>React: ArticleResponse
    React-->>Author: ✅ Article published!

    Note over KAFKA,NS: Phase 3: Async Event Processing (5 parallel consumers)

    par AI Auto-Summarization
        KAFKA->>AIS: Consume ArticleCreatedEvent
        AIS->>AIS: Chunk content for LLM
        AIS->>AIS: Call Claude/OpenAI API<br/>Prompt: "Summarize this article..."
        AIS->>AIS: Generate vector embedding<br/>(for semantic search)
        AIS->>PG: UPDATE articles<br/>SET summary = {ai_summary}<br/>SET embedding = {vector}
        AIS->>KAFKA: Publish ArticleSummarizedEvent
    and Search Index Update
        KAFKA->>SS: Consume ArticleCreatedEvent
        SS->>SS: Build search document<br/>{title, content, tags, author}
        SS->>SS: Add to Knowledge Graph<br/>BFS: find related articles by tags
        SS->>SS: Index in Elasticsearch<br/>Custom analyzer for relevance
    and Analytics Update
        KAFKA->>ANS: Consume ArticleCreatedEvent
        ANS->>ANS: Update author stats<br/>(article count, streaks)
        ANS->>ANS: PriorityQueue.add(article)<br/>for trending calculation
        ANS->>PG: INSERT INTO article_stats
    and Auto-Tagging
        KAFKA->>AIS: (Same event, different consumer group)
        AIS->>AIS: LLM auto-suggest tags<br/>Compare with existing tags
        AIS->>KAFKA: Publish TagSuggestionsEvent
    and Notify Followers
        KAFKA->>NS: Consume ArticleCreatedEvent
        NS->>PG: SELECT followers of author
        NS->>NS: CompletableFuture.allOf()<br/>Send notifications in parallel<br/>(Virtual Threads - Java 21)
        NS->>NS: In-app notification + Email
    end

    Note over Author,NS: ✅ Article is now searchable, summarized, indexed, and followers notified
